# The TRT engine as the probe's fp16 reference, 2026-11-18.
# engine_ref= is the app's own UpscalePytorch (backend=tensorrt); when absent the probe falls back
# to the torch model. Feasibility was demonstrated first: the engine built standalone returns
# (1,3,2160,3840) fp16 on cuda and matches the app's own ungated render at share 0.0% (peak 6.3).

=== Chainsaw 20 s, adversarial top-13
torch reference:  adversarial 0.110%  control 0.083%  d1 0.000%
TRT reference:    adversarial 0.109%  control 0.080%  d1 0.001%
full fp16 sweep:  0.07546%

=== Violet 20 s, adversarial top-13
torch reference:  adversarial 0.168%  control 0.077%  d1 0.095%  d2 0.168%  own defect 0.044%
TRT reference:    adversarial 0.216%  control 0.078%  d1 0.139%  d2 0.216%  own defect 0.081%
full fp16 sweep:  0.07345%

# The engine changes Violet materially (d2 0.168 -> 0.216, own defect 0.044 -> 0.081) and Chainsaw
# barely. The control is still ~6% above the sweep on both clips, so that gap is the pair set (the
# probe re-decides which frames are reused), not the reference.
